# Stack
- Next.js 15 (App Router, Server Components, Server Actions), TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, lucide-react, date-fns + date-fns-tz (timezone **Asia/Riyadh** for all display and slot math), zod for every input.
- Supabase: Postgres, Storage (private bucket `retiree-docs`), Realtime **Broadcast**, `pg_cron` + `pg_net` for the minute tick.
- Daily.co: REST API (rooms, meeting tokens) server-side; `@daily-co/daily-js` call frame client-side.
- Deploy on Vercel.

# Architecture
- **No auth.** Persona id comes from the URL (`/phone/[personaId]`, `/ops/[operatorId]`). Validate it exists server-side on every request.
- **All DB access server-side** via `lib/supabase/admin.ts` (service role). Never import the service role key into client components. The browser uses the anon key **only** for Realtime Broadcast subscriptions.
- Domain logic lives in `lib/domain/*` (pure TS + DB calls), one module per area: `invitations`, `applications`, `review`, `availability`, `bookings`, `sessions`, `feedback`, `reports`, `payments`, `settlement`, `settings`, `notifications`, `audit`, `clock`, `jobs`. Server Actions and route handlers are thin wrappers.
- `lib/domain/clock.ts`: `getAppNow()` reads `app_settings.demo_clock_offset_seconds` (cache ≤ 2s). All rules use it.
- `lib/domain/notifications.ts`: `notify(personaId, {title, body, link})` inserts the row and broadcasts on `persona:{id}`. Also `notifyOperators()`.
- `lib/realtime.ts`: server broadcast helper; client hook `usePersonaChannel(personaId)` that shows the banner and calls `router.refresh()`; global channel `demo` for `clock.changed`, `settings.changed`, `data.reset`.
- `lib/domain/jobs.ts`: `processDue()` exactly as DEMO-SPEC §9; idempotent; exposed at `POST /api/jobs/tick` (header `x-cron-secret`).
- Multi-step state changes (e.g. pause retiree → cancel bookings → refund → notify) run in one function and must be safe to retry.
- Use Postgres constraints as the last line of defence (the exclusion constraint prevents double booking; handle its error as "This slot was just taken").

# Folder layout
```
app/
  page.tsx                       # demo home
  phone/[personaId]/...          # super-app shell + opportunities (seeker + retiree)
  phone/page.tsx                 # splash → welcome → mock Nafath
  ops/[operatorId]/...           # ops console
  tech/page.tsx                  # tech config
  api/jobs/tick/route.ts
  api/sessions/[bookingId]/event/route.ts
components/{phone,ops,shared,ui}/
lib/{copy.ts,supabase,domain,realtime.ts,daily.ts,format.ts}
scripts/seed.ts
supabase/migrations/
```

# Conventions
- Money: numeric SAR, display `SAR 150` (no decimals unless needed).
- Dates in UI: `Tue 11 Nov, 18:00` (Riyadh). Relative times use app time.
- IDs in URLs: personas use slugs; other entities use UUIDs.
- Loading and empty states on every list. Optimistic UI is not needed; refresh after actions.
- Keep components small; no file over ~300 lines.
- Write a short `README.md` section for anything that needs a manual setup step.
